	// schema.prisma
// Single-file version — everything merged from the modular prisma/ files.

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "mysql"
}
// enums.prisma
// Every enum used across the platform, defined ONCE.
//
// Fixes applied vs. the original file:
// - BookingType, BookingStatus, LeaseStatus, AuditAction, OfferStatus,
//   IoTDeviceType, IoTDeviceStatus existed as 2-3 conflicting copies each.
//   Values were merged (union) so nothing already modeled is lost.
// - BillType / BillStatus were dropped: UtilityBillType / UtilityBillStatus
//   already cover the same ground (ESTATE_DUES, MAINTENANCE, SECURITY,
//   WASTE, etc.) and nothing in the schema referenced BillType/BillStatus.
// - DeviceType / DeviceStatus were dropped: they duplicated
//   IoTDeviceType / IoTDeviceStatus and were never referenced by any model.
// - `enum BlockchainNetwork` collided with `model BlockchainNetwork`
//   (Prisma doesn't allow two top-level declarations to share a name).
//   The enum was never used as a field type anywhere, so it's renamed to
//   BlockchainNetworkType and kept in case you want a network-category
//   filter later.
// - LedgerCategory was referenced by LedgerAccount.category but was never
//   defined anywhere — added with standard chart-of-accounts values.
// - MaintenancePriority, MaintenanceStatus, VendorJobStatus are new:
//   the Maintenance and Vendor domains were requested in the master
//   prompt but no models for them existed in the uploaded file at all.

